meta {
  name: Backups
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.get_backups?server=s6qivo97hn&refresh=0
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  server: s6qivo97hn
  ~limit: 10
  refresh: 0
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("has the server header fields", function () {
    const m = res.body.message;
    ["environment", "site_url", "last_backup", "overdue", "backup_schedule", "backup_frequency", "backup_retention"].forEach(function (k) {
      expect(m).to.have.property(k);
    });
  });

  test("never sends oci.reason", function () {
    expect(res.body.message.oci).to.not.have.property("reason");
  });

  test("OCI fields when available", function () {
    const oci = res.body.message.oci;
    if (!oci.available) return;
    expect(oci).to.have.property("fetched_at");
    expect(oci).to.have.property("last_confirmed_at");
    expect(oci.backups).to.be.an("array");
    expect(oci.errors).to.be.an("array");
    if (oci.policy) {
      expect(oci.policy.rules).to.be.an("array");
    }
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  The backup policy, recent backup runs, errors and restores for one server.

  **Endpoint:** `GET /api/method/implementor.client_api.get_backups`  
  **Screen:** Backup

  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). Only records of the user's own client company are returned.

  **Query parameters:**

  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `server` | string | yes | `s6qivo97hn` | `name` from Servers. |
  | `limit` | int | no | `10` | Number of runs in `oci.backups`. Default 10 (also used for `0`), max 50. Send a value from 1 to 10: these are served from the background job's 10-run cache. A value from 11 to 50 has its own cache, so the first request (and the first one after 15 minutes) waits on OCI. Negative values are not supported. |
  | `refresh` | 0 / 1 | no | `0` | 1 reads OCI live. Pull-to-refresh only. At most once every 2 minutes per server; extra refreshes within that window get the cached data, or read OCI live if nothing is cached. |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Not used by the app. The server picks the user's company. Disabled by default. |

  **Response:**

  ```json
  {
    "message": {
      "server": "s6qivo97hn",
      "server_name": "hamza-erp-prod",
      "environment": "Production",
      "site_url": "erp.hamza.sa",
      "last_backup": { "at": "2026-11-06T02:00:12+03:00", "state": "confirmed" },
      "overdue": false,
      "backup_schedule": "Daily 02:00 AST, 14-day retention + weekly offsite",
      "backup_frequency": "Daily, 02:00 AST",
      "backup_retention": "14 days + weekly offsite",
      "last_restore_test": "2026-10-15",
      "restores": [
        { "date": "2026-10-15T22:00:00+03:00", "workflow_state": "done", "downtime_window": "22:00–22:30" }
      ],
      "oci": {
        "available": true,
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-06T02:05:00+03:00",
        "policy": {
          "name": "OCI Gold",
          "rules": [
            { "frequency": "daily", "type": "incremental", "keep_value": 2, "keep_unit": "weeks" },
            { "frequency": "weekly", "type": "full", "keep_value": 1, "keep_unit": "months" }
          ]
        },
        "backups": [
          {
            "name": "hamza-erp-prod-2026-11-06",
            "at": "2026-11-06T02:00:12+03:00",
            "expires_at": "2026-11-20T02:00:12+03:00",
            "frequency": "daily",
            "type": "incremental",
            "state": "confirmed",
            "size_gb": 47
          }
        ],
        "errors": [
          {
            "at": "2026-11-05T02:00:05+03:00",
            "message": "The backup did not complete.",
            "resolved_at": "2026-11-05T03:10:00+03:00",
            "resolution": "A later backup completed and was confirmed."
          }
        ],
        "last_confirmed_at": "2026-11-06T02:00:12+03:00",
        "overdue": false
      }
    }
  }
  ```

  **Top-level fields:**

  - `environment`, `site_url`: as in Servers (`environment` is `Production`, `Staging` or `Dev` as stored; either can be null). For the screen header.
  - `last_backup`, `overdue`: the same values and meaning as in Servers / Server Details, whether OCI is available or not: the newest OCI run when OCI data exists, else the time recorded by our team (`state` `recorded`). Read from this call's OCI data, so after `refresh=1` they can be newer than the Servers list.
  - `backup_schedule`: free text written by our team. Can be null. Show it only when `oci.available` is false or `oci.policy` is null.
  - `backup_frequency`, `backup_retention`: short text written by our team, e.g. "Daily, 02:00 AST" and "14 days + weekly offsite". Null until filled in.
  - `last_restore_test`: date of the last restore test (`YYYY-MM-DD`). Can be null.
  - `restores[]`: up to 5 recent restores, newest first. Can be empty.
    - `date`: date-time with offset.
    - `workflow_state`: lowercase code: `requested`, `scheduled`, `in_maintenance`, `verified` or `done`. Can be null.
    - `downtime_window`: free text. Can be null.

  **`oci`:**

  - `available`: false when OCI isn't configured for this server or can't be read. Then `oci` holds only `available`: hide the policy, runs and errors. The reason is logged on the server, never sent to the app.
  - `fetched_at`: when the data was read from OCI, for "Read from OCI today, 02:05".
  - `policy`: null when the server has no backup policy.
    - `name`: e.g. "OCI Gold".
    - `rules[]`: one row per retention rule.
      - `frequency`: `hourly`, `daily`, `weekly`, `monthly` or `yearly`.
      - `type`: `incremental` or `full`.
      - `keep_value`, `keep_unit`: e.g. 2 + `weeks` → "Kept 2 weeks". `keep_unit` is `hours`, `days`, `weeks`, `months` or `years`.
  - `backups[]`: recent runs, newest first, at most `limit`.
    - `at`, `expires_at`: date-times with offset. `expires_at` can be null.
    - `frequency`: the policy rule it came from (`hourly`, `daily`, `weekly`, `monthly`, `yearly`), `manual` for a one-off backup, or null if unknown.
    - `type`: `incremental` or `full`.
    - `state`: `confirmed` (green), `failed` (red), or `running`, `queued`, `deleted` (grey, with `state` as the label). Any other OCI state is passed through in lowercase; show it as grey.
    - `size_gb`: number, or null while the backup is still `running` or `queued`.
  - `errors[]`: one item per failed run, newest first. Built from all runs read from OCI (at least the last 10), not only the ones in `backups[]`. So with `limit` below 10, an error can refer to a run that isn't in `backups[]`.
    - `at`: when the failed run started.
    - `message`: client-safe text. Show it as is.
    - `resolved_at`, `resolution`: when a later run was confirmed, and what fixed it. Both null while unresolved.
  - `last_confirmed_at`: newest confirmed run, for "No confirmed backup for 30 hours". Like `errors`, taken from all runs read (at least the last 10), not only `backups[]`. Null when none of them is confirmed.
  - `overdue`: true when the server has a backup policy (`policy` not null) and there's no confirmed backup in the last 26 hours. Always false when `policy` is null. Show the red alert when true, even if `errors` is empty.

  **Errors:** client API errors have an `error_code`. Auth errors come from Frappe and have none.

  - **401** (no error_code): token expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403** (no error_code): no Authorization header sent.
  - **403** `not_permitted`: not this client's server, or the server doesn't exist.
  - **403** `no_client_linked`: the user isn't linked to any client company.
  - **417** `missing_parameter`: `server` left out.
}
